// What `<<|` hands back for each key a GUI-style editor needs.
//
// Hypotheses DIS-ZYE-001, 002 and 003 (HALLAZGOS.md). Reads nineteen keys and
// prints the code point of each, separated by spaces: the shape of
// zyquality/tui/keys_control.zy, so the case can move there once the findings
// are fixed. check.py sends the keys through a real pty — `--keys` hands the
// program keys that are already decoded, and the decoding is what is asked.
>>| {
    @ _i:1..19 {
        <<| t
        >> ##!t " "
    }
}
